This is the third consecutive run. Between runs, `./run.sh live` re-seeded the demo
corpus and still passed (Part A PASS, 12/12 payloads removed, held-out 3/3). All
three runs produced identical counts — which is what hard-deleting the drill URN
first is for.

The repo path is replaced with <repo>. Nothing else is edited.

What this run establishes, and what it does not, is written up in
docs/false-positive-revert.md.
